        "raw": "<p>One of the things I really like about the SotM: VG is that it keeps track of things that I never would&#39;ve thought to do if I was sitting down to play the card game. &nbsp;I thought I&#39;d make this post for things that caught people by surprise with how they played out in the video game as compared to the card game. &nbsp;Maybe I&#39;m the only one, but I have three right off the bat:</p><p>1) &nbsp;I used Haka of Battle to increase Haka&#39;s next damage by a large amount, but then absentmindedly attacked a flipped Citizen Dawn. &nbsp;On Haka&#39;s next turn, I attacked a citizen and whomped them for a huge amount of damage. &nbsp;Since I hadn&#39;t actually dealt damage to Dawn, the damage to the citizen was my &quot;next damage&quot;. &nbsp;In real life I probably would&#39;ve played it as increasing the damage of Haka&#39;s &quot;next attack&quot;, though seeing it now I know that makes no sense.</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">2) &nbsp;Fanatic was at 1 HP with Aegis of Resurrection and Sacrosanct Martyr in play. &nbsp;I was able to deal myself 5 radiant damage with Sacrosanct Martyr, resurrect to 10 HP, and then deal 5 damage to the enemy. &nbsp;In real life I probably would&#39;ve played that I could only deal myself 1 HP, although I know in the back of my mind that someone can go to negative HP.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">3) &nbsp;Against Omnitron in Wagner Mars Base. &nbsp;Self-Destruct Sequence and one other card were in play when Omnitron played Terraforming. &nbsp;When the AI gave me a choice for order of destruction for the Environment cards it was showing three cards. &nbsp;I actually took a screen shot to report it before I realized that the third card was UNDER Self-Destruct Sequence. &nbsp;I forget what I did, but I assume if I destroyed Self-Destruct Sequence first the card under it would go to the trash and Omnitron would only play two cards. &nbsp;I guess if I was feeling up for a challenge I could&#39;ve destroyed the card under SDS first and then SDS and the other card so Omnitron would play three cards. &nbsp;I definitely wouldn&#39;t have thought that the card under SDS counted.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
