        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-11-11T22:49:17.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Silverleaf\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/48/2332_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Silverleaf:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I seem to remember a charged Omni-cannon getting destroyed and then being replayed with Decommissioned Hardware. It still had all the cards under it, and I would have assumed they'd be destroyed - but the card says nothing about destroying them.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That was covered in a question in the FAQ. &nbsp;The cards under a destroyed Omni-cannon go back to where they came from and are not repositioned under Omni-cannon if it's put back into play. &nbsp;That sounds like a bug.</p>",
