      {
        "id": 120576,
        "name": "AlexxKay",
        "username": "AlexxKay",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/59ef9b/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-11-12T16:45:18.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Chromium_Man\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/858c86/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Chromium_Man:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li>&nbsp;Against Omnitron in Wagner Mars Base. &nbsp;Self-Destruct Sequence and one other card were in play when Omnitron played Terraforming. &nbsp;When the AI gave me a choice for order of destruction for the Environment cards it was showing three cards.&nbsp; …&nbsp; I guess if I was feeling up for a challenge I could've destroyed the card under SDS first and then SDS and the other card so Omnitron would play three cards. &nbsp;I definitely wouldn't have thought that the card under SDS counted.</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Destroying <em>some</em> cards under SDS would lead to a greater challenge.&nbsp; Destroying <em>all</em> of them leads to an instant game over, as it triggers the SDS!</p>",
